{% block title %}Privacy Policy | Ask the Expat Girls {% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <section class="legal-container">

        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p><strong>Last updated: September 2026</strong></p>

        <p>At <strong>Ask the Expat Girls</strong>, we respect your privacy and are committed
            to protecting your personal data.</p>

        <p>This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store and protect your personal
            information when you use our website, create an account or submit a request through
            our services.</p>

        {# ============================================================
       1. WHO WE ARE
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container1">
            <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
            <p>The website <strong>Ask the Expat Girls</strong> is operated by:</p>

            <address>
                <strong>Ask the Expat Girls</strong><br>
                8 rue de Gramont<br>
                64100 Bayonne<br>
                France
            </address>

            <p><strong>Email:</strong>
                <a href="mailto:info@asktheexpatgirls.com">info@asktheexpatgirls.com</a></p>

            <p>For the purposes of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and applicable
                French data protection laws, Ask the Expat Girls is the data controller responsible
                for the processing of your personal data.</p>

            <p>If you have any questions about how we process your personal data, you can contact us at
                <a href="mailto:info@asktheexpatgirls.com"><strong>info@asktheexpatgirls.com</strong></a>.</p>
        </section>

        {# ============================================================
       2. WHAT PERSONAL INFORMATION WE COLLECT
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container2">
            <h2>2. What personal information we collect</h2>
            <p>We collect personal information that you provide directly to us when you use our website.</p>

            <h3>When you create an account</h3>
            <p>When you create a user account, we collect:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>First name</li>
                <li>Last name</li>
                <li>Email address</li>
                <li>Phone number</li>
                <li>Password</li>
            </ul>

            <p>Your password is stored using secure password-hashing mechanisms and is never stored as plain text.</p>

            <h3>When you complete our questionnaire</h3>
            <p>Once you have created an account, you may complete our questionnaire.</p>
            <p>Depending on the information you provide, we may collect information about:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Your nationality</li>
                <li>Your current situation</li>
                <li>Your plans or reasons for moving to France</li>
                <li>The type of assistance you are looking for</li>
                <li>Your preferences or requirements regarding your move to France</li>
                <li>Any additional information that you voluntarily provide</li>
            </ul>

            <p>Please only provide information that is relevant to your request.</p>
            <p><strong>Do not include sensitive personal information</strong>,
                such as information concerning your health, religious or political beliefs,
                sexual orientation, or other sensitive information, unless it is strictly
                necessary and specifically requested by us.</p>
        </section>

        {# ============================================================
       3. HOW WE USE YOUR PERSONAL INFORMATION
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container3">
            <h2>3. How we use your personal information</h2>
            <p>We use your personal information for the following purposes:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>To create and manage your user account;</li>
                <li>To provide access to our questionnaire and services;</li>
                <li>To review and process your request;</li>
                <li>To understand your situation and provide relevant assistance regarding your move to France;</li>
                <li>To communicate with you regarding your account or request;</li>
                <li>To manage and secure our website;</li>
                <li>To prevent unauthorized access, misuse or fraudulent activity;</li>
                <li>To comply with our legal obligations.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>
        </section>

        {# ============================================================
       4. LEGAL BASIS FOR PROCESSING
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container4">
            <h2>4. Legal basis for processing</h2>
            <p>Depending on the purpose of the processing, we process your personal data on the following legal bases:</p>

            <h3>Performance of a contract or steps taken at your request</h3>
            <p>We process information that is necessary to create and manage your account
                and to provide the services or assistance you request.</p>

            <h3>Legitimate interests</h3>
            <p>We may process certain information where this is necessary for the legitimate interests
                of Ask the Expat Girls, such as maintaining the security of our website, protecting
                our services and preventing misuse, provided that these interests do not override your rights and freedoms.</p>

            <h3>Legal obligations</h3>
            <p>We may process or retain certain information where this is necessary
                to comply with applicable legal obligations.</p>
            <p>Where we rely on your consent for a particular processing activity, we will
                ask for your consent separately.</p>
        </section>

        {# ============================================================
       5. WHO CAN ACCESS YOUR INFORMATION
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container5">
            <h2>5. Who can access your information</h2>

            <p>Your personal information is accessible only to people who need it for the
                purposes described in this Privacy Policy.</p>

            <p>Information submitted through your questionnaire may be accessed by authorized
                administrators of Ask the Expat Girls through our administration dashboard.
                This allows us to review and process your request.</p>

our website, such as:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Website hosting providers;</li>
                <li>Email delivery providers;</li>
                <li>Technical and infrastructure providers.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>These providers may process personal data on our behalf and are required to
                provide appropriate safeguards for the protection of your personal information.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       6. HOSTING
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container6">
            <h2>6. Hosting</h2>

            <p>Our website may be hosted by <strong>o2switch</strong>, a hosting provider
                based in France.</p>

            <p>The hosting infrastructure may be used to store and process the personal data
                necessary for the operation of our website, including user account information
                and questionnaire responses.</p>

            <p>We will update this Privacy Policy if our hosting provider or the relevant
                processing arrangements change.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       7. EMAIL COMMUNICATIONS
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container7">
            <h2>7. Email communications</h2>

            <p>We may use email to communicate with you regarding your account, your
                questionnaire or your requests.</p>

            <p>Our website uses <strong>Symfony Mailer</strong> to manage the technical
                sending of emails.</p>

            <p>Symfony Mailer is a software component used by our application to send emails.
                Depending on the SMTP or email delivery service configured for the website,
                emails may be processed by an additional service provider.</p>

            <p>We will identify the relevant email service provider in this Privacy Policy
                if a third-party email delivery service is used.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       8. HOW LONG WE KEEP YOUR INFORMATION
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container8">
            <h2>8. How long we keep your information</h2>

            <p>We do not keep personal information indefinitely. Personal data is retained
                only for as long as necessary for the purposes for which it was collected.</p>

            <h3>User accounts</h3>

            <p>Your account information is retained for as long as your account remains active.</p>

            <p>If your account has been inactive for <strong>12 consecutive months</strong>,
                we may delete or anonymize your account and the personal information associated
                with it.</p>

            <h3>Questionnaire information</h3>

            <p>Information submitted through our questionnaire is retained for up to
                <strong>12 months after your last contact with us or after your request has
                    been processed</strong>,
                unless a longer retention period is required by law or is necessary for the
                establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.</p>

            <p>Once the applicable retention period has expired, your personal information
                will be securely deleted or anonymized where appropriate.</p>

            <p>The retention periods may be reviewed and adjusted where necessary to ensure
                that personal data is not kept longer than necessary.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       9. HOW WE PROTECT YOUR INFORMATION
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container9">
            <h2>9. How we protect your information</h2>

            <p>We take appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect your
                personal information against unauthorized access, loss, alteration, disclosure
                or destruction.</p>

            <p>Access to personal information through our administration dashboard is
                restricted to authorized users.</p>

            <p>Passwords are stored using secure password-hashing mechanisms and are not
                stored in plain text.</p>

            <p>We also use appropriate security measures for the transmission and storage
                of personal information.</p>

            <p>However, no method of transmission over the Internet or method of electronic
                storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       10. YOUR RIGHTS
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container10">
            <h2>10. Your rights</h2>

            <p>Under applicable data protection laws, including the GDPR, you may have the
                following rights regarding your personal information:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Right of access:</strong>
                    you can request a copy of the personal information we hold about you;
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Right to rectification:</strong>
                    you can ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete information;
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Right to erasure:</strong>
                    you can request the deletion of your personal information, subject to
                    applicable legal exceptions;
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Right to restriction:</strong>
                    you can request that we restrict the processing of your personal information
                    in certain circumstances;
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Right to object:</strong>
                    you may object to certain processing of your personal information where
                    permitted by law;
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Right to data portability:</strong>
                    where applicable, you may request to receive your personal data in a
                    structured, commonly used and machine-readable format;
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Right to withdraw consent:</strong>
                    where processing is based on your consent, you may withdraw your consent
                    at any time.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>To exercise your rights, please contact us at:</p>

            <a href="mailto:info@asktheexpatgirls.com">
                    <strong>info@asktheexpatgirls.com</strong></a>

            <p>We may need to verify your identity before processing certain requests.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       11. DELETING YOUR ACCOUNT
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container11">
            <h2>11. Deleting your account</h2>
            <p>You may request the deletion of your Ask the Expat Girls account and the
                personal information associated with it by contacting us at:</p>

            <a href="mailto:info@asktheexpatgirls.com">
            <strong>info@asktheexpatgirls.com</strong>
            </a>

            <p>When you request deletion, we will delete your personal information unless
                we are legally required or otherwise permitted to retain certain information.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       12. INTERNATIONAL DATA TRANSFERS
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container12">
            <h2>12. International data transfers</h2>
            <p>We aim to use service providers that provide appropriate protection for
                personal data.</p>

            <p>If personal data is transferred outside the European Economic Area (EEA),
                we will ensure that the transfer is carried out in accordance with applicable
                data protection laws and that appropriate safeguards are in place.</p>

            <p>This Privacy Policy will be updated where necessary to provide information
                about relevant international data transfers and the safeguards used.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       13. COOKIES
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container13">
            <h2>13. Cookies</h2>
            <p>Our website may use cookies and similar technologies.</p>

            <p>Some cookies may be necessary for the website to function properly, including
                cookies required for authentication and security.</p>

            <p>Other cookies, such as analytics or advertising cookies, may require your
                consent before they are used.</p>

            <p>For more information about the cookies used on our website and how to manage
                your preferences, please see our
                <strong>Cookie Policy</strong>.
            </p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       14. COMPLAINTS
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container14">
            <h2>14. Complaints</h2>
            <p>If you believe that your personal data has been processed in a way that does
                not comply with applicable data protection laws, you have the right to lodge
                a complaint with the French data protection authority:</p>

            <address>
                <strong>Commission Nationale de l'Informatique et des Libertés (CNIL)</strong><br>
                3 Place de Fontenoy<br>
                TSA 80715<br>
                75334 Paris Cedex 07<br>
                France
            </address>

            <p>You can find further information on the CNIL website.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       15. CHANGES TO THIS PRIVACY POLICY
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container15">
            <h2>15. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes to
                our services, our data processing practices or applicable laws.</p>

            <p>When we make changes, we will update the
                <strong>"Last updated"</strong>
                date at the top of this page.</p>

            <p>We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically to stay informed
                about how we protect your personal information.</p>
        </section>


        {# ============================================================
       16. CONTACT US
       ============================================================ #}

        <section class="legal-container16">
            <h2>16. Contact us</h2>
            <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or about how your personal
                information is handled, please contact us:</p>

            <address>
                <strong>Ask the Expat Girls</strong><br>
                8 rue de Gramont<br>
                64100 Bayonne<br>
                France
            </address>

            <p>
                <strong>Email:</strong>
                <a href="mailto:info@asktheexpatgirls.com">
                    info@asktheexpatgirls.com
                </a>
            </p>
        </section>
    </section>
